{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454901-ideas-for-chantry-defences","id":1454901,"title":"Ideas for Chantry defences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-14T13:24:12-07:00","id":1454901,"title":"Ideas for Chantry defences","content":"I'm looking for ideas in general, as nothing in particular is jumping out at me right now.<br /> Hmm. Also, how would you tailor a set of defences against each clan? Particularly the Setites (just buying a ton of flood lights might help, but the Divine Hand path could counter than if they have any lector priests)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-14-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T17:41:26-07:00","id":1454924,"title":"","content":"Tremere chantry design is a place that is often lacking in V:tM. Admittedly most of my knowledge comes from V20 or earlier.<br /> <br /> To add some character to the chantries in my games, I try to theme them so that they synergize with the primary thaumaturgy paths taught there or at least known by the senior members. For example the Green Path allows you to control plants, so the chantry would have an atrium, attached green house, or even have trees growing through the structure. If the tremere know neptunes might then the chantry would have elaborate water gardens or be based in a light house next to the sea. Once you have worked out the theme and what would be required to augment or otherwise improve the use of certain paths, you will get a lot of detail down about the chantry.<br /> <br /> This synergy with known paths or rituals also means that things like using the path of conjuration to make loads of permanent silver items becomes viable if you have were-critters in the area. Most STs would raise an eyebrow at the notion of having sterling silver door knobs, security pad keys, or just enough silver plating to cover an entire hallway floor to ceiling, but with the conjuring it is a non-issue.<br /> <br /> For non-magical defenses, it is really just about creating a check list for how some one would attack a chantry. <br /> <br /> 1. The outer walls and roof are fire proof materials and hopefully thick enough to be bullet proof against anything smaller than a 50 caliber. The thickness of the roof and walls also means you can't easily use a drill and pesticide sprayer to &quot;inject&quot; a gaseous form Protean user into the building.<br /> <br /> 2. There should be either a raised floor plan or cement barriers (planters) so that a vehicle can't ram its way inside or park close enough to do damage with a bomb.<br /> <br /> 3. Have a sprinkler system installed on the roof so you can essentially hose down the house exterior or the surrounding yard to deal with fires. Also there is something funny about having a group of enemies acting all badass threatening to attack the house, when suddenly the house starts hosing them down.<br /> <br /> 4. Install halon fire suppression systems inside the house, it will put out fires without causing water damage to books and will kill anything that requires air to breath.<br /> <br /> 5. Have a secure garage so that anything that tries to hop a ride on a Tremere vehicle doesn't just get easy access, of course the vehicle should be warded as well.<br /> <br /> 6. Exterior Security cameras with thermal imaging can let you know at a decent distance if a group of vampires are squading up nearby.<br /> <br /> 7. Have the interior design of the chantry reflect the notion of choke points and security doors. Just because you managed to get past the front door and initial warding doesn't mean there aren't another half dozen security doors to get past before you can get your fangs into a Tremere. You should need to go through an airlock of sorts at all major entry points, preventing anyone from just rushing a door.<br /> <br /> 8. Have plans in place for each level of threat. Yes this does create a scenario where vampire mages are holding some what goth fire drills for when rival clans, shifters, or mortals attack. But having the everyone know what they are supposed to do in those situations can make or break the effectiveness of many defenses. Its great to have several steel security doors, but not so much if no one remembers to lock them.<br /> <br /> 9. Have an escape route preplanned. Eventually the walls fail, the gate is breached, and the chantry is lost, but that doesn't mean you have to go down with the ship. Rituals are useful here, teleport to a true friend is good for those that can cast it, alternatively the one where you can pass through a wall is great if the chantry basement is next to a major sewer tunnel.<br /> <br /> 10. Be a bad loser, part of your escape plan has to include a self destruct for the chantry. This means that Tremere secrets never fall into their enemies hands and potentially the enemy that breached the chantry die as a result. Considering how dickish this can be you want something like falls in line with the theme of the chantry. <br /> <br /> Of course all of the aforementioned is based off the idea that your enemy knows exactly where the chantry is, how to get there, and can essentially lay siege to it. An alternative is to have a fake chantry that is connected to the real one. This way after battering down the doors and tanking the wards, all the attackers find is destroyed arcane lab equipment and piles of vampire ash. They think the Tremere killed themselves and destroyed their own chantry, they write it off as a victory and go on to the next target. All the while the Tremere are in the real chantry just keeping a low profile until things blow over.<br /> <br /> A variant of the fake chantry is the death trap chantry where you actually design and include Saw movie or james bond death traps into the fake chantry building. Sure the enemy will observe the Tremere coming and going from this house or this houses garage, but they have no way of knowing that the tremere travel by tunnel into a house across the street or simply deep underground. Thus they expend huge amounts of resourses and many cainite lives breaking in, all the while the Tremere continue their research.<br /> <br /> The important thing to realize about vampire chantries is that they only really have to hold out for a night cycle, unless they are very remote, the siege has to stop for the day, at which point Tremere ghouls or just normal mortal workmen can come in during the day and repair damage or reset traps. In one game I ran the players designed the traps so only about a third of them were active on any given night, thus you had at least three nights worth of sieging before most of the traps were cleared out, then they would activate the self destruct once the enemies were about to breach the final fake chantry sanctum security door.<br /> <br /> Just a few thoughts off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T10:08:02-07:00","id":1454977,"title":"","content":"Indeed there's a lot of conventional/easy/inconspicuous methods to fortify the chantry, like a raised floor plan.. You don't necessarily need an impossing, castle like defence.<br /> Nightingale floors (deliberately squeeky floors). Curtains over doorways. courtyards, good doors, Smooth outer walls with not much to grab onto. one way glass. small/barred windows or strategically placed spikey plants are all very inconspicuous methods to deter intruders. Being in a 'nice' neighbourhood also helps a lot, though doesn't make for great eating. The Tremere are going to want to own or monitor every nearby building with a good view of the chantry to make it hard for fellows to spy on the chantry. At the least, Make sure their mortal employees live there or something.<br /> <br /> Of course, , pillboxes, murderholes, machicolations, &quot;airlocks&quot;, hounds, arsenals of security cameras... they all work too. Trapdoors and hidden flamethrowers are probably more trouble than they're worth. In storming buildings in, say, a counter-terrorist operations, attackers ideally want to fight downwards: secure the exterior, sneak some guys on the roof, and fight down. Of course the Tremere are usually going to be too connected to worry about a SWAT team, and I feel vampires, with their inexhaustible stamina, probably mitigate some of the disadvantages of fighting up.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are very good at making money. They don't need lots of ghouls or dominated servants, they can work with private security.<br /> <br /> <br /> RE stealing magic.<br /> So, real life hermetics/alchemists did not compile their work in an easily understandable manner. Archaic languages, ciphers, strange euphemisms, non-standard notations, misinformation, terrible handwriting; You aren't going to find an easy book on how to work Lure of Flames. These books aren't going to make a lick of sense to those who aren't properly initiated high enough into the Tremere and who haven't received the knowledge to understand the references and dismantle the ciphers. You are never going to let anyone photocopy these works either.<br /> <br /> RE:Settites<br /> All setites should strive to become thaumaturges. Except maybe warriors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}